\description{
This is market-on-open or limit-on-open, the Atlas's G1. UBI places it at \code{at_time} while the pre-open is collecting orders, answering HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed}, or at once, with the broker's answer, when collection is already open. Only NSE and BSE equities and exchange traded funds, until 09:10 for a limit and 09:05 for a market order, and NSE stock and index futures, until 09:07 and 09:05, have a pre-open; UBI refuses anything else with HTTP 400 rather than send it into continuous trading, and refuses stop orders and \code{ioc} too. It does not check that a future is the current month's, the only one with a pre-open. Times follow the instrument's exchange trading calendar, so on a weekend or an exchange holiday the order waits for the next trading day's pre-open. Keep the \code{parent_id} from the answer, since nothing reaches a broker until then.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
